\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{A fiber basis for the connection weight}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{Choose a basis of the fiber #{F} in the
[connection background](fdip-006D). In the resulting basis of
#{K=F^E}, the pointwise weight #{(Wa)(e)=w_ea(e)} is the
block-diagonal operator #{\operatorname{diag}(w_eI_F)}. The twisted
incidence #{d_U}, its adjoint and the precision #{Q_U} are defined
without that basis. Real and complex fibers use the same formula;
the complex case is the underlying real quadratic form of the
unitary representation.}
